  "note": "Broiler.VM's half of SJL-3: the cut-over's evidence, taken from clean checkouts of the after commit 49ea00e (source-revision) and, for the rules and the engine-level vectors, of 141f7cd, whose product sources are 49ea00e's, against bundle sjl-0-001's base 0087e8d7: identity, closures in three modes with rule I7's identity as the collector recorded it when they were taken (closures/admitted-packages.json, the package then on the committed feed, packed from Broiler.JS 93df3fd; the feed was re-pinned afterwards to the package as published), whole-suite test262 in both forms with its (c') re-runs at both commits, the fuel-parity twins, the differential cross-check, the rules, the engine-level vectors and the simplification check. measurement/ is part C's sub-bundle, of the class measurement, with its own manifest.txt and hashes.txt, and is not hashed here. Each run's commit and binary hashes are in its own log; the README says which commit each was taken at. (Noted 2026-10-20: collect.py has changed since this bundle was collected. With decision-rule-revised-2026-10-20.md, part C's rule revised after its first run was seen, it gained step measure-revised and the options --numref, --default-branch and --check-only, and no other step changed. The hash under retained, 26cbc3b43dc292a31ea4fdb36062f8c382ec91589a0a60db64e694d102ab517e, is the collector that collected this bundle; the collector as the revised rule's commit holds it has SHA-256 23c4f29cad9a4c59c3ffd0446976dde342b2dd3cfcdde85e1d49039729103b58, and measurement-revised/manifest.txt names it by blob as arm A holds it. The files added with the revised rule - the rule itself, transcript/ and revision-check/, the check seen before the rule was written, with its own README - are not hashed here.) (Noted 2026-10-20, after part C was taken under decision-rule-revised-2026-10-20.md: measurement-revised/ is that run's sub-bundle, of the class measurement, at arm A ebf93cd3e8fba11002f3da563b13b32ca54afe32 against arm B 0087e8d7, and is hashed by its own hashes.txt, not here; its README, written after the run, is in neither. The bundle's README.md reads it in a new section 10, with a dated note on its State paragraph and a dated pointer at the end of its section 7, so the README's hash under retained, ee2baf141de1ed7319909476873861b96d64ee42d0d39cd5224fc0824caa5764, is the README as this bundle was collected, as the collector's is.)",
